.nh
.TH "PB-DEVICE-REVOKE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-device-revoke - Disconnect and revoke a device


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb device revoke <device> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Disconnect and revoke a device

.PP
Disconnect and revoke the selected enrollment. Existing device credentials lose authority; the confirmation code confirms this account-level removal.

.PP
Devices are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected device, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-device(1)\fP
